    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end. The app derives read-only response fields via an OpenAPI-generated DTO layer + MapStruct mapper, and persists owner data across the separate `POST`/`GET` requests, so the change touched four layers:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional input, enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `salutation` field to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` on build.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so the title survives from create to read.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the derived mapping: `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`. (`title` itself maps automatically by name between DTO enum and entity String.)\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table. The test suite runs on hsqldb.\n\nThe new `Cp45Tests.coreComposesSalutation` passes (`title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 `salutation=\"DR who\"`), and the full suite is green: **56 tests, 0 failures**.",
